# Optional modules

Copy a module only when the app needs it. When you skip one, also delete its references
from `ApiBase`, `http_client.dart`, `main.dart`, `GoRouterApp`, and `pubspec.yaml`.

## Auth (login, token, 401 re-login)

- Files: `reference/lib/Models/User/UserAuthModel.dart` (adapt to your backend), auth branch in
  `ApiBase.requestApi` (`skipAuth`), token in `ApiBase.getHeader()`, 401 handling in `http_client.dart`.
- Routes: login screen in `AppRoutes.dart`; splash decides login vs home.
- Session globals (settings, current branch...) loaded once after login, cleared on logout (`state-and-cubit.mdc`).
- Without auth: remove `UserAuthModel`, `skipAuth`, the auth header, and the 401 branch.

## Local cache

- Files: `Helper/connection/cash/` (`CashLocal`, `model/`), cache flags in `ApiRequest`.
- Package: `shared_preferences`.
- Use for read-mostly lists that should show instantly. Never cache writes or user-private data on shared devices.
- Without cache: keep the `ApiRequest` flags at `false`; the cache folder can stay unused or be removed.

## Pagination / infinite lists

- Files: `Widgets/LoadingListView/` (`LoadingListView`, `LoadingListController`, `ShimmerList`), `<Feature>FilterModel`.
- Packages: `shimmer`.
- Controller pattern: `loadMore()` → if `!loading && hasMoreItems` then `filter.page++` and fetch; append results.

## File uploads

- Files: `Helper/ApiServices/Base/FileUpload.dart`, `ApiBase.uploadFile`, `RequestType.upload`.
- Packages: `http_parser`, `path` (+ `image_picker`/`file_picker` as needed).
- Not supported on web without changes (uses `dart:io` `File`).

## Deep links / share links

- Files: `AppRoutes/Base/DeepLinkingRoutes.dart` (or a `DeepLinkService` that maps an incoming URI to a route).
- Every deep-linkable screen must load from path parameters alone (`routing.mdc`).
- Platform setup: Android intent filters / iOS associated domains / web URL strategy.

## Demo / dummy data

- Pattern: a `Dummy<Feature>Data.dart` next to the model + a policy that returns dummy data when a
  flag is on or the request fails in debug.
- Must be off in release builds; never mix dummy data into a successful real response.

## Helpers you may drop

`Helper/Map+ext.dart`, `Helper/ApiServices/Api.dart`, `Helper/ApiServices/Apis/ApiStatus.dart`,
`nb_utils`, `rxdart`, `logging` — keep only if code actually uses them.
